From 969a9063a8cf8d557d2505f6c7424fee62c03776 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 13:57:29 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 09/10] D-51: the design's hold-down replay weighs the stack as
 the flight does
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

src/design/warnings.ts holdDownRelease replays Simulation.stepPrelaunch
for the Build's `noLiftoff` warning, and tests/design-warnings.test.ts holds
the two to one verdict at the edge of liftoff. The flight now weighs the
stack with the pad's normal gravity (J2 and the Earth's turn at the WGS-84
pad); the replay takes the site (its latitude and altitude) and does the
same, instead of μ/(R + h)². The edge-of-liftoff test passes (5 vehicles,
static T/W 0.90-1.06).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018CKDnUSFqs1bpw8C2bZmPj
---
 src/design/warnings.ts        | 19 +++++++++++--------
 tests/design-warnings.test.ts |  2 +-
 2 files changed, 12 insertions(+), 9 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/design/warnings.ts b/src/design/warnings.ts
index d1e80d4..c9bffdc 100644
